<title>SOUTH AFRICA: GFSA'S O'Okiep Q2 net profit after Q1 loss.</title>
<headline>GFSA'S O'Okiep Q2 net profit after Q1 loss.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-June versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Net profit before capital spending 14.73 vs 6.83 loss</p>
<p>    Capital spending			  2.07 vs 2.63</p>
<p>Copper recovered</p>
<p>     in concentrate (tonnes)	     5,610 vs 5,101</p>
<p>Copper in blister</p>
<p>     produced (tonnes)		     9,428 vs 7,904</p>
<p>    Copper in blister sold (tonnes)    8,434 vs 5,812</p>
<p>    Tonnes milled			  427,000 vs 396,000</p>
<p>    Sales					95.98 vs 64.67</p>
<p>    Cost of sales			    80.91 vs 71.36</p>
<p>Full name: O'okiep Copper Co Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it had embarked on a strategy of securing a minimum copper price of $2,200/t through the use of derivatives. It said currently 15 percent of own production between July 1997 and April 1998 has been secured.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
